SECTION 1 (new TCA 39-17-1328(b)): No person shall sell or transfer ownership of a firearm, or purchase or obtain ownership of a firearm, unless one (1) of the following applies:
SECTION 1 (new TCA 39-17-1328(b)(1)): The seller or transferor is a gun dealer;
SECTION 1 (new TCA 39-17-1328(b)(2)): The seller or transferor makes the sale or transfer to or through a gun dealer and obtains a receipt;
SECTION 1 (new TCA 39-17-1328(b)(4)): The transferor is transferring ownership of the firearm to a family member by gift, bequest, or inheritance; the transferee is not prohibited from possessing a firearm under this part; and the transferee is at least eighteen (18) years of age; or
SECTION 1 (new TCA 39-17-1328(c)): Any person who intentionally violates subsection (b) commits a Class B misdemeanor and shall be fined not less than five hundred dollars ($500) nor more than ten thousand dollars ($10,000) and may be imprisoned for a period not to exceed nine (9) months. A person convicted under this section is prohibited from possessing a firearm for a period of two (2) years.
